BP55 in place of CVA6's BHT/BTB/RAS (BP55 harness, option A of cva6/README.md).

Everything is under `ifdef BP55_PRED`, which only the bp55 variant defines
(cva6/cva6.sh adds +define+BP55_PRED and an unmodified copy of rtl/bp55.sv);
without the define the RTL is unchanged.

- core/cva6.sv: branchpredict_sbe_t gets a 174-bit field bp55 = {type, f_ckpt,
  f_meta}, which travels with every instruction through the instruction queue,
  ID, the scoreboard and the branch unit's operand register to commit; the
  frontend gets the record of the instruction in the branch unit and of the one
  at commit.
- core/frontend/instr_queue.sv: carries the record per instruction (no-C path).
- core/frontend/frontend.sv: BP55 instance and prediction at the pre-decode
  stage, frontend repair redirect, EX and commit repairs, training; see the
  comment block in the file.

